    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1982835777361846577",
      "url": "https://x.com/ShaneHummus/status/1982835777361846577",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ShaneHummus/status/1982835777361846577",
      "text": "We had a retreat in the Philippines\n\nrented out an entire private island for the team\n\n- fire dancing \n- beach villas \n- peacocks everywhere \n\nwent up to this spot called the sea of clouds where you're literally above the clouds in the mountains\n\nAND THEN THREE (3) earthquakes hit while we were there\n\nlast retreat two and a half years ago we swam through a venomous sea snake mating ground without knowing it. captain got his head smashed trying to dock in sudden high waves\n\nbetween those retreats? nothing \nzero incidents in Davao City for 30 months straight\n\ni fly my team down and nature decides to test us again\n\n- 6 people died in the city from the quakes\n- poorly constructed buildings\n- air conditioners falling\n\nwe were safe on the island but i'm supposed to be the leader keeping everyone comfortable\n\ninstead i'm watching the ground move like we're on a boat\n\nbut this is why we do these things\n\nyou can't build a real team over Zoom calls and Slack messages\n\nwe did team building exercises. \nhired a specialist who made us fish balls out of containers using chopsticks. \nsounds weird but it forced us to figure out communication and strategy under pressure\n\nasked questions. learned how people actually think when problems hit\n\nremote work is efficient but there's something that only happens face to face\n\nmy team has a different appreciation for each other now\n\nworth every earthquake",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
